{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Components","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It keeps a copy of the graph to look vertices up through the graph’s own vertex indices, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" hashes nothing on a graph whose indices are its vertices. The copy shares"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage (copy-on-write), so making it is O(1), and later changes to the original do not affect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the result. The cost comes later: while the result is alive, the next mutation of the original"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copies the whole graph, as it would with any other copy. Drop the result, or keep only what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you need from it ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array(components)"},{"type":"text","text":"), before mutating the graph."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A component’s slice keeps the indices of the flat storage it is cut from, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"CompressedSparseRow.successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does: use "},{"code":"first","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", iteration or "},{"code":"Array(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"code":"[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because its type names the graph’s type, a result cannot be returned through an existential","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any DirectedGraph"},{"text":": call it from a generic function (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"some DirectedGraph"},{"text":") instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"A partition of a graph’s vertices into components, in a documented order: a collection of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components, each a slice of vertices in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, with an O(1) ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"component(of:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/endIndex","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/startIndex"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(checked:)","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(of:)","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/component(ofIndex:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Subscripts","anchor":"Subscripts","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components\/subscript(_:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/